# skill-package-freshness gate — enforcement sentinel (#2656)
#
# This committed marker governs whether the .skill package content-freshness CI gate
# (`deploy.sh --check-package-freshness`, i.e. Check 7's content-hash verdict) BLOCKS
# or merely REPORTS when a rostered skill's compiled `.skill` package is stale versus
# its source (SKILL.md / references/). The probe reads this file directly, so the
# sentinel is load-bearing on its own; the thin CI workflow
# (skill-package-freshness.yml) additionally consumes the probe's exit code.
#
# The first non-comment, non-blank line is the mode token:
#   warn      → report only (exit-0); a STALE package is surfaced but does not block.
#   enforce   → block on a STALE package (exit-1 propagates to the CI caller).
#
# Ships DORMANT (warn) during the calibration window, per the warn-mode-initial
# posture. The introducing release `governance-ci-gates` dogfoods this gate green on
# its own PR (its #1632 eval-writer reference edit + rebuild is the live regression
# signal). Flip the token below to `enforce` after a >=3-day warn-log review with zero
# false positives (dep #2159 — Check 7's non-reproducible-archive false-positives —
# is CLOSED) AND after the operator adds the `skill-package-freshness` job to
# `required_status_checks` (branch protection — the out-of-tree enforcement surface).
# No code change is needed to graduate.
#
# (Token-flagged rather than presence-flagged so the file can ship now — the docs
#  reference it — while the gate stays non-blocking; mirrors close-completeness.enforce.)
warn
